NegroniMetal changes to the ios-flame 745c434 Metal frontend (MIT), on top of 0001. The CoreAnimation fixes that
Chlorophyll (ry-diffusion/Chlorophyll 787338f, MIT) found on iOS 18 / Adreno 630, written again for this frontend
(docs/reviews/bergamota-chlorophyll-2026-10-25.md section 3 item 1; its section "Ported"):
- Device SPI that the 20H392 _MTLDevice answers with NULL (targetDeviceInfo: {0, 0, device name}, Metal's own fallback)
  or not at all (dedicatedMemorySize 0, sharedMemorySize = physical memory, as UniXNU NativeMetal (MIT);
  recommendedMaxWorkingSetSize = half of it).
- A refused or nil render pipeline and a refused draw are skipped and logged once; the command buffer goes on
  (draws after a refused pipeline are skipped too: the runtime keeps the previous pipeline). Telemetry row N counts them.
- DontCare colour attachments of textures that are not IOSurfaces start cleared to zero (CA's rounded-corner masks).
- After a completed command buffer, each IOSurface its GPU work wrote gets a write lock + unlock (seed bump), except in
  backboardd; NEGRONIMETAL_SEED_BUMP=0/1 overrides.
- native_bridge_metal_progress: committed/completed/pending counts and the oldest pending age, for the plugin's GPU watchdog.

